  {
   "key": "federal-representatives-482",
   "date": "2008-05-29",
   "house": "representatives",
   "question": "The majority voted in favour of a [motion](http://www.openaustralia.org/debates/?id=2008-05-29.37.1) to read the bill for a third time.(Read more about the stages that a bill must pass through before becoming law [here](http://www.peo.gov.au/learning/fact-sheets/making-a-law.html). ) This means that the majority agree with the bill and that it will now be sent to the Senate for their consideration. _Background to the bill_ The [bill](http://www.aph.gov.au/Parliamentary_Business/Bills_Legislation/Bills_Search_Results/Result?bId=r2992) was introduced to increase the [Medicare](http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Medicare_%28Australia%29) levy surcharge threshold to $100,000 for individuals and to $150,000 for families.(Read more about the bill in its [bills digest](http://parlinfo.aph.gov.au/parlInfo/download/legislation/billsdgs/T2NQ6/upload_binary/t2nq63.pdf;fileType=application/pdf) (73.8 KB).)",
